<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch-significant-figures" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>🎭 Significant Figures</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      The title of this chapter was inspired by Ian Stewart's <em>Significant Figures: The Lives and Work of Great
      Mathematicians (2017)</em>, whose title makes a clever literary use of the mathematical term
      <xref ref="gls-significant-figure" text="custom">significant figure</xref>.
      I encountered Stewart's book while sorting through my father's belongings shortly after his
      passing in the summer of 2026, and its title struck me as a perfect match for the title of this chapter.
    </p>
    <p>
      Here, <em>significant figures</em> refers to influential mathematicians and scientists who built the historical
      narrative of scientific discovery and curiosity. I retain the title with gratitude to Stewart for the
      inspiration, and to my Dad for leaving the book where I could find it.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <xi:include href="./pre-quantum/sec-pre-quantum.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="./sec-post-quantum.ptx" />
   
</chapter>
